PATCH 162: the FSG chunk handlers that parse a mission's <battle>.FSG into the model/unit list
(asm 0xd7b5/0xd7da/0xd7e1/0xd87f/0xd8a9/0xd8d3/0xd8e9), dispatched by FUN_0000_d501 through the
7-entry table DAT_2000_a9e6@0x2a9e6 {SHDR->d7b5, DCBS->d7e1, TERM->d7da, PATH->d87f, STMP->d8e9,
PINF->d8a9, BINF->d8d3}.  Reached ONLY on the ACCEPT mission cascade (BATTLES->OK->ACCEPT) via
4754->d501; NOT reached by any of the 19 verify flows -> behaviour-neutral for verify.

Two asm-verified defect classes, both proven against re_out/fist_dat_image.bin:

(1) HOST-POINTER-INTO-DOS-REGISTER (patch 077/146/156 class) in the THREE already-promoted handlers
    (d7b5, d7e1, d87f).  Each INT-21h AH=3f read set the DX reg-file slot to `&DAT_2000_...`, a HOST
    pointer whose low-16 (what fist_dos.c R_DX reads) is garbage.  The asm puts a DGROUP near-offset in
    DX:  d7b5 `mov dx,0xe982`; d7e1 `mov dx,0xe9be`/`0xe9c2`/`0xe9c0`; d87f `mov dx,0x7d40`.  Fixed to
    store the literal offset.  (The lseek branches already passed the value DAT_2000_a97a correctly.)

(2) FOUR handlers Ghidra never promoted (d7da TERM, d8a9 PINF, d8d3 BINF, d8e9 STMP) -- reached only
    through the cs-vtable-style d501 dispatch, so fist_icall_near(0,off) TRAPPED them (returned 0) and
    their FSG chunk was silently skipped.  Reconstructed instruction-faithfully from the image and
    fmap-registered at their linear addresses:
      d7da TERM: byte[DGROUP:0xe974]=1; clc.
      d8a9 PINF: if byte[0xe975]==1 read word[0xe97a] bytes -> DGROUP:0x85b6 else seek-forward.
      d8d3 BINF: read word[0xe97a] bytes -> DGROUP:0x79cd (the .KLC/battle-info name buffer);
                 byte[DGROUP:0x7a13]=1.
      d8e9 STMP: if byte[0xe975]==1 read word[0xe97a] bytes -> DGROUP:0x9338 else seek-forward.
    All use bx=handle DAT_2000_a970, DS=DGROUP(0x1c00) (the ambient reg-file DS d501 leaves set), and
    the DX buffer as a value (never a host pointer).

NB the DCBS record reader FUN_0000_d81e (asm 0xd81e) still carries a di/unaff_CS base-loss (the model
record struct offset is FUN_1000_b1a2's DI return, which the __allregs model dropped) -- a separate
deliverable; it only matters if the AZER1 mission carries DCBS records.

